Subject: [PATCH 1/2] ci: fetch full history so v2 git blame dating works in
 tests

A shallow checkout makes every model line look newer than the source
claims, so the v2 drift tests saw no drift and 16 tests failed in CI
while passing locally. Reproduced with a depth 1 clone; a full clone passes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TmNHAejFyUhXr6HmiYVSp3
---
 .github/workflows/tests.yml | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/tests.yml b/.github/workflows/tests.yml
index 95fc2df..effe6b4 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/tests.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/tests.yml
@@ -19,6 +19,9 @@ jobs:
       - uses: actions/checkout@v7
         with:
           persist-credentials: false
+          # v2 reconciliation dates model lines with git blame; a shallow clone makes every
+          # line look newer than the source claims, so drift tests need full history.
+          fetch-depth: 0
       - uses: actions/setup-python@v6
         with:
           python-version: "3.12"
